      "writtenOn": "2026-08-13T09:33:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right. I checked the caller side (powerStateChanged), and it was indeed calling createSensors synchronously, which resulted in three redundant rescans during a BMC reset.\n\nWe will use a static boost::asio::steady_timer in powerStateChanged to debounce the createSensors execution by delaying it for 1 second. With this change, createSensors will be executed exactly once after the initial burst of power state syncs.",
      "parentUuid": "585ada05_e6fd977a",
